Nethack has way too many sword artifacts.  Yeah, they're prominent in
mythology, but there's a full fourteen artifact swords, and ten of
various other weapon types.  I call that discrimination, and I call for
greater equality of weapon types.  And the first way to solve that is
by introducing polearm artifact weapons.  I suggest this because there
are none in NH as of yet; because legendary spears have their place in
mythology, not only swords have this distinction; and because I really
like long pointy weapons.

I can name a few examples off the top of my head that would make good
artifact weapons:

Gungnir, Odin's spear - Bonus to hit and damage, and returns to the
hand after thrown.  Simple enough, and Valkyries could get it as a
favored weapon maybe. (They already have Mojo though, which doesn't
help.)

The Longibunne Spear - This was referenced very obscurely in "Final
Fantasy Tactics", and was probably in another FF game.  Breaks armor
and shields on contact.  This would make an awfully fun low-level
weapon, albeit a risky one.

Gae Bolg - Cuchullain's spear.  Dunno the big details about it, though.
 But given the mythology, could make a good Knight weapon?

The Spear Luin - Another Celtic spear, blade constantly burning hot,
wielded by Lugh.  Possibly the same as Gae Bolg, but hey, NHINRL
already.  (And Hooray for Knight-ly stuff.) Fire-elemental polearm,
anyone?

I'm sure there's other mythical/fictional polearms that could be thrown
into NH.  I'd love to see wieldable, viable, non-trash (i.e. Trollsbane
or Ogresmasher) artifacts that aren't swords, to give the discerning
hacker a little more variety.  Anyone know of any that I'm blissfully
ignorant of?


